sequenceDiagram
    participant A as Session A
    participant DB as jobs table
    participant B as Session B

    Note over A,B: Scenario 1 - FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED
    A->>DB: BEGIN
    A->>DB: SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED LIMIT 5
    DB-->>A: rows 1-5 (locked, txn open)
    B->>DB: BEGIN
    B->>DB: SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED LIMIT 5
    Note right of B: rows 1-5 locked - skip them, don't wait
    DB-->>B: rows 6-10 (locked)
    Note over A,B: Neither session blocks
    A->>DB: COMMIT
    B->>DB: COMMIT

    Note over A,B: Scenario 2 - plain FOR UPDATE
    A->>DB: BEGIN
    A->>DB: SELECT ... FOR UPDATE LIMIT 5
    DB-->>A: rows 1-5 (locked, txn open)
    B->>DB: BEGIN
    B->>DB: SELECT ... FOR UPDATE LIMIT 5
    Note right of B: rows 1-5 locked - wait for them
    A->>DB: COMMIT
    DB-->>B: rows 1-5 (same rows, now released)
    Note over A,B: Session B sat blocked the whole time
